WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.650
One instruction turns a crashed robot into a successful delivery.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:12.459
Forkline is a remix studio for Twitch: change one step, replay both futures, and see
exactly when they split.

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:18.544
A viewer starts with the command on screen: exclamation mark fix, zero, one, W.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.162
Here is that repair as a local preview.

00:00:23.182 --> 00:00:27.960
I select original zero, step one, and replace Forward with Wait.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.548
Blue and coral run on the same clock.

00:00:30.568 --> 00:00:37.392
Blue hits the closed gate on beat three; coral arrives on beat four, crosses, and
delivers on beat seven.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.531
This is Twitch's own chat, in Antivex's channel.

00:00:42.551 --> 00:00:51.284
A logged-in viewer sends exclamation mark fix, zero, one, W. Forkline receives the
real message and creates a credited remix.

00:00:51.304 --> 00:00:54.651
On the same clock, the original stops at the gate.

00:00:54.671 --> 00:00:57.920
The viewer's wait crosses it and delivers at beat seven.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:12.314
On the third challenge, Rae fixes the turn, then Sol continues Rae's version and
fixes the timing.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:15.227
Those names are fictional example credits.

00:01:15.247 --> 00:01:19.032
Both contributions stay visible in the parent-and-author trail.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:27.735
Copy a replay link to reopen that whole trail, or copy the OBS URL for a clean
stream stage.

00:01:27.755 --> 00:01:30.713
Viewers use their existing Twitch login.

00:01:30.733 --> 00:01:39.336
The studio listens as a read-only guest, credits explicit fix commands using Twitch
identity tags, and counts each message ID once.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:48.912
Codex built the deterministic engine, original maps, SVG studio, and Twitch adapter
during this hackathon.

00:01:48.932 --> 00:01:57.705
Here is the actual build thread: a browser check exposed a same-tab replay bug;
Codex added the hash-change handler and the check passed.

00:01:57.725 --> 00:02:00.304
The session ID and source are public.

00:02:00.324 --> 00:02:04.144
Open Forkline, listen to your channel, and make one change.

